> Armor
> an uncursed +1 robe
>   (improves cast rates on hard spells)
> an uncursed +0 cloak of magic resistance

Magic resistance is not optional, it is essential.  Without it, you can
be zapped around by teleport traps (not a major problem), your armor is
vulnerable to polymorph traps (okay THIS is a major problem), and
you're very vulnerable to enemy spells, including Destroy Armor and
(ugh) Touch of Death.  Genociding liches will help you for a while, but
it'll eventually come back to haunt you when you when the Wizard starts
calling, not to mention Astral.

Since you already have reflection, I'd suggest making or wishing for
GDSM when you get the chance, especially since it'd let you keep your
cool cloak of displacement.  (I would have used that first wish for
GDSM, its usefulness cannot be overestimated.)  However, that would
make you a little vulnerable to level drainers like barrow wights and
vampires.


> a blessed magic marker (0:13)

Magic markers can be recharged once, and with a blessed scroll you'll
always get 50 charges out of it.  Consider trying to write one (since
it's on your discoveries list) with your remaining juice.


