Actually, reflection is never necessary.  Magic resistance provides
some damage protection against breath weapons like from winter wolf
cubs, and unless you encountered them in a wide-open, lit area you can
probably handle those by retreating to a corner and taking them one at
a time in melee.


> I think I'd choose a ring of slow digestion before
> the GDSM on my next wish, though), and where do I
> need to go from here?

Unlike Rogue (where slow digestion was all but essential), it can
actually get in your way in Nethack, although your amulet of magical
breathing helps with that problem.  You'll have a near inexhaustible
food supply from the barracks of the castle alone, and there's always
monster snacks.  If you keep moving quickly (as melee characters
should) I think you'll be okay, especially with those food rations.

Magic resistance is too useful to do without, without it or polymorph
control it's only a matter of time before that +6 elven mithril is just
so much scrap.  Be on the lookout for ways to get that, and be careful
with liches and golden nagas until you do.  (I forget if the healer
nemesis is a spellcaster?)

